cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VSA Operations findings, please cite this work. HybridBigInt SIMD achieves 17.2× speedup for ternary vector operations."
title: "Trinity B007: VSA Operations for Ternary Computing — HybridBigInt SIMD"
abstract: "We present Vector Symbolic Architecture (VSA) operations optimized for ternary computing using HybridBigInt SIMD. Key innovations include: (1) HybridBigInt SIMD structure with 32 limbs, 16 trits per limb; (2) Ternary bind/unbind operations (XOR-like for {-1,0,+1}); (3) Bundle2/Bundle3 majority vote operations; (4) Permutation with cross-limb carry for cyclic rotation; (5) Cosine similarity for ternary vectors ([-1,+1] range); (6) 30% noise resilience in retrieval tasks. Results: 17.2× speedup on ARM NEON for cosine similarity, linear scaling with vector width. Pure Zig implementation with platform-specific SIMD optimizations (ARM NEON, x86 AVX2 planned). Complete algorithm pseudocode, truth tables, and benchmark results. Applications include text encoding, episodic memory retrieval, and hyperdimensional computing for AI agents."
